Let a missing desktop-GL library disable the demos that need it.

`dependency('gl')` is required, so a system whose GL stack is EGL/GLES only
— no libGL, no gl.pc — cannot configure this project at all. Marking it
optional and a disabler makes meson skip exactly the targets that list
dep_gl (the GLX and desktop-GL EGL demos) and keeps eglinfo, the GLES
demos and vkgears, none of which reference it.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
 dep_m = cc.find_library('m', required : false)
 dep_winmm = cc.find_library('winmm', required : false)
 
-dep_gl = dependency('gl')
+dep_gl = dependency('gl', required : false, disabler : true)
 
 dep_epoll = dependency('epoll-shim', required : false)
 dep_gles1 = dependency('glesv1_cm', required : get_option('gles1'))
